-- title:
--   Strong approximation away from a split place, double-coset form
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be negative and let $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated rational quaternion algebra. Let $O\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order in the sense of the predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathbb{Z}$ such that $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ contains a non-zero non-unit. Let $y$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^f_{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that for every height-one prime $w\neq v$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ to the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{I},z_{J},z_{K})$ on pure tensors, the element $\varphi(y_w)$, where $y_w$ is the image of $y$ under the base change of evaluation at $w$, has reduced norm $x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a x_I^2-b x_J^2+ab\,x_K^2$ equal to $1$. Then there exist $\beta\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ and units $g,u$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^f_{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $u$ stabilises, under multiplication, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in O$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele; $g_w=1$ for every $w\neq v$; and $y=\beta\, g\, u$, where $\beta$ is inserted via the diagonal map $\mathbb{H}^{\times}\to(\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^f_{\mathbb{Q}})^{\times}$ coming from $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$.
--
--   This is the double-coset form of strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite rational quaternion algebra relative to the places $\{\infty,v\}$, Eichler's condition being supplied by the splitting of $\mathbb{H}$ at $v$: every finite idele whose local reduced norms away from $v$ are $1$ lies in $\mathbb{H}^{\times}\cdot\mathbb{H}_v^{\times}\cdot\widehat{O}^{\times}$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, to produce elements of the away-from-$v$ unit group with prescribed reduced norm or prescribed behaviour on coset graphs, and in the analysis of Hecke double cosets at the level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one.lean

